  "quizQ1QuestionTitle": "Gaussian Elimination: Pivot & Elimination",
  "quizQ1Prompt": "In the matrix below, the first pivot is at cell (1,1). Which elementary row operation eliminates the first entry in row 2?",
  "quizQ1Explanation": "The first entry in row 2 is 2, and the pivot is 1. To obtain 2 - 2 \\cdot 1 = 0, apply R_2 \\leftarrow R_2 - 2R_1.",
  "quizQ1Hint": "Subtract a multiple of the pivot row from the target row to create a zero.",
