  "quizQ2Hint": "A zero pivot cannot eliminate other rows; swap with a row having a non-zero leading entry.",
  "quizQ2Feedback0": "Adding row 2 would also create a non-zero pivot, but this question asks specifically for a row swap.",
  "quizQ2Feedback1": "Swapping rows 1 and 2 moves the non-zero entry 3 into the pivot position.",
  "quizQ2Feedback2": "Changing row 2 leaves the zero at (1,1) unchanged.",
  "quizQ2Feedback3": "Scaling row 3 leaves the zero at (1,1) unchanged.",
  "quizQ3QuestionTitle": "Pivot Normalization (Scaling)",
  "quizQ3Prompt": "The pivot entry in row 2 is -3. Which operation scales this row to produce a leading one (1)?",
  "quizQ3Explanation": "Multiply every entry in row 2 by −1/3: (−3) × (−1/3) = 1.",
  "quizQ3Hint": "Multiply the entire row by the reciprocal of the pivot value.",
  "quizQ3Feedback0": "Adding row 1 destroys the leading zero and does not normalize this pivot.",
  "quizQ3Feedback1": "The reciprocal of −3 is −1/3, so their product is 1.",
  "quizQ3Feedback2": "Multiplying −3 by 3 gives −9. Use the reciprocal instead.",
  "quizQ3Feedback3": "Swapping rows changes positions; it does not scale −3 to 1.",
  "quizQ4QuestionTitle": "Matrix Rank and Zero Rows",
  "quizQ4Prompt": "What is the rank (number of linearly independent rows) of this echelon form matrix?",
  "quizQ4Explanation": "The matrix is in echelon form with 2 non-zero pivot rows and 1 all-zero row. Therefore, rank(A) = 2.",
  "quizQ4Hint": "Count the number of non-zero rows in row echelon form.",
  "quizQ4Feedback0": "The zero row contributes no pivot. Matrix size alone does not determine rank.",
  "quizQ4Feedback1": "There are two pivot rows in this echelon matrix.",
  "quizQ4Feedback2": "The second non-zero row contains another pivot and must also be counted.",
  "quizQ4Feedback3": "Rank zero would require every entry of the matrix to be zero.",
  "quizQ5QuestionTitle": "Determinant of a Triangular Matrix",
  "quizQ5Prompt": "The determinant of an upper triangular matrix equals the product of its main diagonal entries. What is det(A)?",
  "quizQ5Explanation": "For any triangular matrix, det(A) is the product of entries along the main diagonal: 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 24.",
